  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a persistent upward bias when recent history shows a strong uptrend (e.g., >38 EUR) and low sentiment; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 1-2 EUR.",
    "When sentiment is near zero or slightly positive, the model fails to capture immediate mean reversion after price spikes, resulting in over-forecasting volatility peaks.",
    "Forecasts show significant lag in reacting to negative sentiment shifts; when sentiment drops below 0.25 following a high, the model continues to project higher prices than actual outcomes.",
    "The model systematically underestimates downside risk during periods of mixed sentiment (0.00-0.25) and recent volatility, leading to overly optimistic short-term projections.",
    "In high-volatility regimes (history range >10 EUR), the model's 30-day forecast becomes increasingly inaccurate as it smooths out erratic true outcomes that correlate with sentiment spikes."
  ]
}
